# Mockingbird copies the copiable values of a token (ruling): Bot2's Lingering Souls leaves two 1/1 white Spirit tokens with flying. Bot1
# casts Mockingbird with X = 0 (one mana spent) and copies one: mana value 0 (a token has no mana cost, CR 202.3). The result is a
# card, not a token, named Spirit: a white 1/1 Spirit Bird with flying. It is not a token, so it does not cease to exist
# (CR 111.7) and, had it left the battlefield, would be a Mockingbird card again.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mockingbird
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Lingering Souls
Island x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lingering Souls.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Mockingbird.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Spirit Token#1)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Island; Spirit Token
Bot1.Battlefield.Spirit Token.Subtypes = Bird; Spirit
Bot1.Battlefield.Spirit Token.Keywords = Flying
Bot1.Battlefield.Spirit Token.Colors = White
Bot1.Battlefield.Spirit Token.Token = (absent)
Bot2.Battlefield = Mox Pearl; Mox Jet; Mox Ruby; Spirit Token; Spirit Token
